  "description": "SADVUS crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C114 H109 Gd12 N20 O58 1+,6(H2 O1),C2 H3 O2 1-,x(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd9 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd10 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd11 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd12 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.470-4.576 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.56-134.97°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd12(H2L1)4(μ3-O)4(μ3-OH)4(CH3COO)15]·(CH3COO)·(CH3OH)6 (EA: C122H136Gd12N20O66). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
